# Spec authoring

## Naming

- File pattern: `<Flow>_<Template>_Test.spec.ts` (e.g. `FieldValidation_CovoroTemplate_Test.spec.ts`)
- Test titles use domain language with template, field, condition, and outcome:
  - Upload: `Excel upload · Covoro | Document | Invoice Number | empty → error file`
  - UI: `Create Invoice UI | Document | minimum length (1 char) → validation error`

## Structure

- Keep specs thin: import test data → loop → call one helper function.
- One end-to-end expectation per test.
- Use `test.describe.configure({ mode: "parallel" })` unless serial order matters (e.g. sanity).
- Set explicit `test.setTimeout(...)` only for long backend waits (submit/delivery, dropdown suites).

## Template constants

- Declare `const TEMPLATE = "Covoro"` (or OMN primary template name) in upload specs.

## npm scripts for targeted runs

- Covoro: `npm run test:covoro`
- UI manual: `npm run test:ui`
- Sanity: `npm run test:sanity`

## Agent prompts for this layer

- One spec file or one test case per agent turn (`incremental-agent-edits` rule).
- Prefer skills (`add-field-validation-case`, `add-conditional-validation-case`, `add-submit-test-case`, `generate-excel-from-testcase`, etc.) over broad “fix all specs” prompts.
- Oman conditional upload: only `*-OM` rule IDs — see `conditional-validation-oman` rule.
- Explore helpers via graphify query — do not paste entire spec files into chat (`agent-token-scope` rule).
